/** User manual — owner / customer edition. Content only; rendered by views/manual.php.   GAS-CP-R20-002
 *  Each section: id, title, body (array of paragraphs — plain text, or ['ul' => [...]] / ['ol' => [...]] / ['fig' => file, 'cap' => caption] / ['tip' => text]). */
return [
  'title' => 'Customer Portal — User Manual (owners and customers)',
  'lede'  => 'How to follow your vessels and projects, approve documents, raise tickets, accept service reports and keep track of what changed — from any browser, on a computer, tablet or phone.',
  'sections' => [
    ['id' => 'signin', 'title' => 'Signing in', 'body' => [
      'Delivery notes by e-mail (v1.267.0): Golden A/S can send you a delivery note for acceptance by e-mail. Open the personal link in the message, confirm your mailbox with the 6-digit code sent to the same address, check the list of goods and sign on the screen — or choose «Not received as listed» and write what is missing or damaged. No portal account is needed, and you receive a confirmation with the signed note.',
      'Georgian in the app (v1.265.9): the Golden A/S Customer app 1.0.16 offers Georgian (ქართული) in its language selector, as the portal does. The installed app takes the new version by itself the next time it is opened with a connection.',
      'Georgian — third delivery (v1.265.2): now also in Georgian — service and inspection reports, work orders, timesheets, tickets, tasks, the equipment register, the HR Assistant, assessments, the knowledge base, portal requests, the process flow, the working calendar, projects with drawings, submittals and reports, and the pages a customer sees. About 31 % of the texts of the portal are translated; the rest is still shown in English.',
      'Georgian — ქართული (v1.265.0): Georgian is a new language of the portal; choose it in the language selector or on My account. The translation is delivered in stages. First stage: menu, sign-in, authenticator and passkeys, sessions and devices, dashboard, notifications, In / Out, planning and wellness. A text not translated yet is shown in English, so nothing is missing; each following stage replaces more of the English. The assistant answers in Georgian when the portal is set to Georgian. The apps follow in a later stage.',
      'Acceptance by e-mail link — «Access Denied» fixed (v1.259.1): a customer who opened the acceptance link of a service report (or of another document sent for acceptance) and pressed a button — send the code, confirm the code, accept or dispute — got the page «Access Denied – GoDaddy Website Firewall», block FBP007. The acceptance page told the browser to send no referrer, and the website firewall refuses every form sent without one. The page now sends the referrer to the portal only (never to other sites), so the buttons work; the same correction is on the newsletter unsubscribe page. A customer who met the error opens the same link again — nothing was lost and the link is still valid.',
      'Devices on My Account (v1.259.0): (1) My Account shows the card «Devices that signed in to this account» with every browser and phone you have used, when it was first seen and when it last signed in; the browser you are using is marked. (2) «Forget» removes a device from the list, so that a later sign-in from it is announced to you again; to sign a device out use «Sign out everywhere». (3) A wrong authenticator code typed in a mobile app counts toward the account lock like a wrong password (five in a row, 15 minutes).',
      'Security notices on your account (v1.258.0): (1) A wrong password typed in a mobile app counts like one typed in the portal: five in a row lock the account for 15 minutes. (2) When your account signs in from a browser or a phone you have not used before, you get the notification «New sign-in to your account» with the device and the address. If it was you, there is nothing to do; if not, change your password, choose «Sign out everywhere» under My Account and tell the administrator.',
      'Language no longer changes when you open a notification (v1.248.3): links made by a colleague who works in another language carried that language, and opening one — from the bell, a message or an e-mail — switched your portal to it and saved it on your profile. Now, while you are signed in, the language changes only when you choose it in the 🌐 selector. If your language was changed this way, choose yours once in the selector; it is saved and stays.',
      'App updates (v1.226.0): when a new version of the Golden A/S Customer app is in the App Store or on Google Play, the app shows «A new version of the app is available» with an Update button, and you receive a notification and an e-mail with the link. If your phone updates apps automatically, you do not have to do anything.',
      'Notification state in the apps (v1.224.1): on the settings screen of each app (More › Settings; in the Customer app More › About), under the version, the app now names the store build that is installed and where notifications stand — «on», «not allowed — switch on in the settings of the phone», «not in this build — update the app from the store», or the reason of a failure. The version on the first line is the version of the screens, which follow the portal; the store build is what is installed on the phone.',
      'Push notifications (v1.224.0): after you update the Golden A/S Customer app (1.0.13) from the store and sign in, the phone asks once «Allow notifications?». Choose Allow to be told when an approval is asked, an offer or document is ready, a report waits for your signature or a ticket is answered. You can stop them in the settings of your phone.',
      'Push notifications (v1.223.0): the Golden A/S Customer app can notify you on your phone when an approval is asked, a new offer or document is ready, a report waits for your signature or a ticket is answered. A tap opens the right page. It starts with the next version of the app; you allow or stop notifications in the settings of your phone.',
      'Golden A/S Customer on the App Store (v1.212.3): the app was released on the App Store on 21/11/2026. In the Mobile apps block of the home page and the sign-in page the App Store tile is now a working link with its QR code.',
      'App icons with the app name (v1.210.4): the icons of Golden A/S Service, Golden PM and Golden A/S Customer now carry a gold tab with SERVICE, PM or CUSTOMER at the lower right, as Golden HR already had with HR — the four apps are told apart at a glance on the phone. Apps added to the home screen from the browser show the new icon after they are added again; apps installed from the App Store or Google Play show it with their next store update. Nothing else changes in the apps.',
      'Customer app 1.0.11 — demonstration (v1.210.3): an account that Golden A/S has marked as a demonstration account opens the app on an invented fleet with example reports, offers, tickets and documents. Nothing shown there belongs to a real customer and nothing done there is sent to Golden A/S. Normal customer accounts are not affected.',
      'Customer app 1.0.10 — photos on tickets (v1.210.2): in Tickets › New ticket and in the reply of a ticket, the 📷 button now opens the phone’s own picker — Take Photo, Photo Library or Choose File. On iPhone the app could stop when a photo just taken was confirmed, and the ticket was lost; this is corrected. Large photos are reduced on the phone before they are sent (location data removed, as before). What you type in a new ticket — vessel, category, priority, subject and description — is kept on the phone until the ticket is sent, so it is still there if the app is closed or restarted in between; it is removed when the ticket is sent or when you sign out.',
      'First sign-in — choose your own password (v1.208.0): when your account was opened, or your password was reset, by an administrator, the first sign-in stops at the page Choose your own password. Type a new password twice — at least 10 characters with a letter and a digit, without the name of your e-mail address and different from the one you were given — and press Save and continue; the portal opens right after. Until then nothing else opens. In the apps the same happens on the sign-in screen: the two fields New password / Repeat appear, fill them in and press Sign in again. A sentence of three or four words is easy to remember and hard to guess; Golden A/S never asks for your password.',
      'Projects — open issues (v1.205.0): the filter bar of Projects has a new field Open issues: With open issues, Status: Open, Status: In progress, Overdue or High priority — the list then shows only the projects that have such an issue. Every project of the list that has open issues shows a block Open issues beside Offers and Tasks, with the count (open · in progress · overdue in red); unfold it for the list — number, issue and priority, sub-project, category, to be done by, assigned to, due date and status — without opening the project. The number opens the issue in its sub-project. With the filter set the block opens by itself.',
      'Tab menus on a gold band everywhere (v1.202.1): every tab menu of the portal — Recruiting (Vacancies · Applications · Online events · Talent pool), Payables, HR, Inventory, Settings and all the others — now stands on the same pale gold band with a gold line as the subproject menu, and the tab you have open is navy with white text. On pages where the open tab was not marked before (Recruiting, for example) you can now see which one you are on.',
      'Sign-in page centred (v1.201.1): the sign-in card, the language selector, the «Need access?» line with «Request portal access» and the Mobile apps block now stand in one centred column of the same width; the access line wraps onto two lines instead of pushing the card to the left.',
      'Sign-in page — request portal access (v1.199.1): under «Need access? Ask your Golden A/S project manager to invite you.» there is now a link «Request portal access». It opens the Customer Portal access page of the Golden A/S website in a new tab, where a customer without an account can read how access is given and ask for it.',
      'Mobile app on the home page and the sign-in page (v1.199.0): at the bottom of the home page, and under the sign-in form, a Mobile apps block shows Golden A/S Customer with a QR code for Google Play (Android) and one for the App Store (iPhone). Point the phone camera at the code, or tap the tile when you are on the phone, install the app and sign in with your portal account. Until Apple releases the app its App Store tile is grey and reads «In review at Apple»; «Open the web app» opens the same app in the browser.',
      'Subproject menu on a gold band (v1.198.6): on the subproject page the menu (Process, Sections, Works … Contacts) now stands on a pale gold band with a gold line under it, and the tab you have open is navy with white text. The menu is the same as before — only its background changed, so it is easy to tell apart from the figures and tables below it.',
      'Customer app — one name, Golden A/S Customer (v1.198.5): the app for owners and captains is now called Golden A/S Customer on the phone, inside the app and in Google Play and the App Store (on the phone it was shown as Golden A/S Portal). Sign-in, passkeys and data are unchanged. The store apps show the new name with their next update; a web app already on a home screen keeps the old name until it is removed and added again.',
      'Customer app — Golden A/S logo as the icon (v1.198.4): the Golden A/S Customer app (phone app and the web app added to the home screen) now shows the Golden A/S logo on navy with the gold bar as its icon, the same as the Service and PM apps, instead of the gold G mark. Nothing changes inside the app. A web app already on a home screen keeps the old picture until it is removed and added again; the store apps get it with their next update.',
      'Filters — type to pick from the list (v1.195.3): a drop-down became a type-to-search list only when it had more than eight entries, so a short filter such as Vessel on the purchase orders opened as a plain list. Now, in every filter bar of the portal, a drop-down with four or more entries opens with a search box: click it, type a few letters, press Enter or click the entry. The Vessel and Supplier filters of Purchase orders and of the Pipeline board are always searchable, whatever their length. Fixed choices of two or three entries (for example Purpose) stay plain lists.',
      'Signed out on the screen when the idle time runs out (v1.185.1): the portal has always ended your session after the idle time (30 minutes unless your administrator set another value), but a page left open stayed on the screen and you only saw the sign-in page at your next click — so it looked as if you were still signed in, and whatever was on the page stayed readable. Now the open page itself goes to the sign-in page with the message "You were signed out after a period of inactivity" as soon as the time is up, and also when you come back to the tab. Work in another tab of the portal counts as activity for all tabs. Save your form before leaving the desk: an unsaved form on an expired page is lost.',
      'Signed out when you come back (v1.127.7): for your security the portal signs you out when its last tab has been closed for more than about 45 seconds — the same as closing the browser. If you then open the portal again you go straight to the sign-in page with the message "The browser was closed — for your security you were signed out"; sign in again and continue.',
      'Your Golden A/S project manager creates your account and sends you the address of the portal, your e-mail address as user name and a first password. Open the address in any modern browser (Edge, Chrome, Safari, Firefox) — nothing is installed on your device.',
      ['fig' => 'c-login.jpg', 'cap' => 'The sign-in page — e-mail and password, then the six-digit code from your authenticator app'],
      ['ol' => ['Enter your e-mail address and password and press Sign in.', 'The first time, the portal asks you to set up two-factor authentication: scan the QR code with an authenticator app (Microsoft Authenticator, Google Authenticator, Authy …) and type the six-digit code it shows.', 'On every later sign-in, type the current six-digit code from the app after your password.']],
      'Your session ends after 30 minutes without activity (your administrator may set another value), after 10 hours at most, and when you close the browser — reopening the window or restoring the tabs brings you back to the sign-in page, never straight into the portal. A session is also tied to the browser it was opened in. Under My account › My sessions you can sign out of every browser at once; do that and change your password if you suspect that someone else used your account. Too many wrong passwords lock the account for a short time — wait and try again, or contact your project manager.',
      ['tip' => 'Lost your phone or the authenticator app? Ask your Golden A/S project manager to reset two-factor authentication; you will set it up again at the next sign-in.'],
      'If the portal ever shows "The portal is locked", its service contract is being renewed — nothing of yours is lost; contact your project manager and try again later.',
    ]],
    ['id' => 'layout', 'title' => 'Finding your way around', 'body' => [
      'The portal has three parts: the top bar, the menu on the left and the page itself. Under the top bar a clock strip shows the time in UTC, Greece (home, framed in gold), the UAE, the United Kingdom, Italy, the Netherlands, Germany and Dallas, 24-hour, with the date and ISO week. The Greek clock carries a small weather badge; click any city for sunrise / sunset, daylight length, the conditions now, today\'s minimum / maximum, rain chance, wind and the hourly forecast.',
      ['fig' => 'c-weather.jpg', 'cap' => 'The clock strip with the weather badge and the pop-over for Athens'],
      ' The top bar shows the bell with your unseen changes, the theme switch (light / dark), the gear for your account settings, the language as a two-letter code (EN, GR, IT, UA, BG — English, Ελληνικά, Italiano, Українська, Български) and, at the far right, the sign-out icon (⇥). The menu is grouped like your work: Fleet (vessels and projects), Work (tickets, work orders, service reports), Commercial (offers, owner approvals) and Library (documentation, IT & cybersecurity, support). On a phone the menu folds behind the ≡ button.',
      ['fig' => 'c-dashboard.jpg', 'cap' => 'The dashboard — fleet progress, what needs your attention, this week across the fleet and your vessels'],
      ['ul' => ['Gold badges on a menu entry count items waiting for you — tickets waiting for your reply, documents to approve, offers to decide.', 'A gold dot on a menu group means something changed there that you have not seen yet (see Notifications).', 'Long lists — projects, vessels, service and inspection reports, offers, approvals, tickets — show 25 rows per page with a pager under the table (25 / 50 / 100 per page); filters and totals always cover the whole list.', 'Breadcrumbs above every page title lead back to the vessel or project.', 'Every list has filters at the top; the Apply button runs them, Clear resets.']],
      ['ul' => ['Any table sorts on click: click a column header to sort by that column, click again for the opposite direction. Numbers and dates are recognised.']],
